<!--
  `F-158` — the mark inside the floating bubble, and the notification's small
  icon.

  ## Why it is the slash and nothing else

  Same reasoning as `ic_launcher_foreground.xml`: at 26 dp floating over
  somebody else's screen, any detail beyond one stroke collapses into a smudge.
  The slash is the whole brand at this size.

  ## Why one drawable serves two very different jobs

  This file is used twice — as the bubble's glyph, where the `fillColor` below
  is honoured, and as the ongoing notification's `setSmallIcon`, where it is
  **not**: Android throws away the colour of a notification small icon and
  renders the alpha channel alone, tinted by the system. That is fine here and
  it is the reason this is a solid path rather than a stroked one. A stroked
  or multi-tone mark would work in the bubble and come out as a grey blob in
  the shade.

  ## Why the fill is ink and not gold

  Because it is drawn on `swip_bubble_disc`, which is gold. In the shade
  this colour is discarded entirely - Android renders a notification small
  icon from its alpha channel alone and tints it - so the one file can be
  ink in the bubble and correct in the status bar at the same time.

  Geometry is notification geometry, not launcher geometry: a 24 unit viewport
  with the mark inside the middle 20, because the status bar crops to a circle
  and a shape that runs to the edge loses its ends.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">

    <path
        android:fillColor="#060507"
        android:pathData="M13,3 L18.4,3 L11,21 L5.6,21 Z" />
</vector>
